# {{ name }}

Demo deployed via [demo-tools](https://github.com/BosTheCoder/demo-tools).

- **Stack:** {{ stack }}
- **Deploy target:** {{ target }}
{% if target == "pages" -%}
{% if publish_mode == "root" -%}
- **Local dev:** `just dev` — serves these files on http://localhost:{{ internal_port }}. No build step and no container: what you edit is what ships.
{% else -%}
- **Local dev:** `just dev` — serves the built output. `just build` first, or run your bundler's own dev server for hot reload.
{% endif -%}
- **Deploy:** `just deploy` — {% if publish_mode == "root" %}pushes `main`; Pages serves the repo root{% else %}builds, then pushes `dist/` to `gh-pages`{% endif %}. Then it registers the Pages config, the `CNAME`, and the DNS record.
- **Live URL:**
  - https://{{ name }}.github.io (until a custom domain is attached)
  - Put a hostname in a `CNAME` file at the repo root and `just deploy` points it at Pages. DNS-only — a proxied record breaks GitHub's certificate issuance.
- **First deploy?** The HTTPS certificate can take up to an hour. `just status` shows its state, which is the usual answer to "why does http work but https doesn't?".
- **No server here.** `just secret` deliberately fails: anything this page can read, a visitor can read. Public config belongs in the source; a real credential needs `DEMO_TARGET=fly just deploy`.
- **Status / logs / destroy:** `just status` / `just logs` (Pages build history) / `just destroy` (disables Pages, leaves the repo).
{% else -%}
{% if stack in ["fastapi", "streamlit"] -%}
- **Local dev:** `just dev` — hot reload via `compose.dev.yml` (your `app/` is bind-mounted, so edits apply without a rebuild; changing `requirements.txt` still needs `just build`).
{% else -%}
- **Local dev:** `just dev` — runs the production image, so a source change needs a rebuild. For hot reload, add a `compose.dev.yml` that bind-mounts your source and runs your dev server; `just dev` layers it automatically.
{% endif -%}
- **Deploy:** `just deploy`
{% if target == "local" -%}
- **Live URL** (Tailscale, tailnet-only):
  - https://{{ tailscale_host }}{{ tailscale_path }}
- **Data:** persists in `./data` on this machine (SQLite). `just destroy` keeps it.
- **Graduate to Fly:** set `target: fly` in `.demo-template-version`, then `just deploy` (serves at https://{{ name }}.fly.dev).
{% else -%}
- **Live URLs:**
  - https://{{ name }}.fly.dev (always works)
{% for h in hostnames -%}
  - https://{{ h }}
{% endfor -%}
  Hostnames come from the `hostnames` list in `.demo-template-version`; `just deploy`
  points each one at this app's IPs and provisions a cert. Set it to the real
  domains for an app that owns them, or `[]` to deploy without touching DNS.
{% endif -%}
- **Stop / start / destroy:** `just stop` / `just start` / `just destroy`
{% endif -%}
- **Update infra files:** `just sync`
